# Architecture

Full detail: `docs/02-architecture.md`.

## Monorepo (current reality)

- One real app: `apps/usr`. Shared UI is `apps/usr/src/components/ui/` — this is the canonical UI library.
- Libs today: `libs/api-client`, `libs/auth`, `libs/shared-types`, `libs/shared-ui`. The role of
  `libs/shared-ui` vs the app UI folder is undecided: do not add components to `libs/shared-ui` until it is.
- Move code into `libs/` only when a second app actually consumes it. Until then, cross-route code lives in
  shared folders of `apps/usr/src/` (`components/`, `lib/`, `hooks/`).
- `apps/adm` and `apps/bus`: status undecided (`docs/09-known-issues.md`). Do not add code there and do not
  import from them until the decision is recorded.
- Nx tag boundaries are not enforced yet (`sourceTag: "*"` in `eslint.config.mjs`). Follow the import direction
  anyway: UI components import nothing domain-specific or data-related; feature code imports UI, data and utils;
  nothing imports from an app into a lib. Cross-project imports use path aliases, never deep relative paths.
- Server-only code is marked `server-only`.

## Route colocation

Every route that owns data or interaction uses this layout. `page.tsx` stays thin. No empty folders.

```text
app/<route>/
  page.tsx      # params, guard, compose components — no logic
  components/   # UI composition for this route (existing convention; do not rename to sections/)
  api/          # functions the screen and hooks call — the only data entry point
  hooks/        # server-state and other hooks for this route
  utils/        # pure helpers for this route
  types/        # types for this route
  mock/         # MOCK ONLY — fake data + fake implementations, same shape as api/
```

- `api/` is the only module sections and hooks import for data. In the mock phase `api/` validates input and
  delegates to `mock/` (fake delay + in-memory data). When the real endpoint exists, only `api/` changes.
- `mock/` has `README.md` and a `// MOCK ONLY` header. Never import `mock/` from sections or hooks.
- New mocks go in `mock/`. Existing mocks in other places (`data/settings-mock.ts`, `home/data/search-mock.ts`,
  `(auth)/api/mock.ts`) are legacy: move them to `mock/` behind `api/` when the route is next touched. All mocks
  are listed as MOCKED in `docs/07-integrations.md`.
- One route uses it → it stays in that route. Two or more routes → the app's shared folders (or `libs/` once a
  second app needs it). `components/ui/` never imports from a route folder.

## SRS service modules

All SRS services (SRV, Rwd, Dsc, Rfl, Msg, Nws, Nwl, Cln) use the same shape so the pattern repeats:

- Routes per actor surface: public site, user panel (پنل عملیاتی کاربر), provider panel (پنل عملیاتی سرویس‌دهنده),
  admin panel (پنل راهبری). Exact route groups: `docs/04-routing.md`.
- One data-access module and one types module per service, shared by all its routes (location confirmed with
  me before the first service is built).
- Cross-service behaviours (approval, soft delete, archive, categories, reasons, reports) come from shared libs —
  see `41-shared-patterns.mdc`. Never re-implement them inside a service.
- Before creating the first module of a new service, confirm names with me and record them in `02-architecture.md`.

## Size

A page or component over ~150–200 lines, or with more than one data fetch plus one non-trivial interaction, is
split per `docs/conventions-large-feature-ui.md`.
